told:_IntellectualProperty_2
	a gist:IntellectualProperty ;
	skos:prefLabel "Mahākāla Pañjarnātha"@en ;
	gist:description """<p>
	Mahākāla Pañjarnātha, or \"Lord of the Tent,\" is the protector of the Hevajra cycle of tantras. The iconography and rituals are found in the eighteenth chapter of the <em>Vajra Pañjara Tantra</em>, an exclusive 'explanatory tantra' to Hevajra itself. It is dated to the late fourteenth or early fifteenth century.</p>"""@en ;
	gist:isCategorizedBy tolx:_WorkType_painting ;
	gist:isConnectedTo told:_HistoricalPeriod_56 ;
	gist:isIdentifiedBy told:_ID_har_82 ;
	gist:isMemberOf <https://w3id.org/treasuryoflives/ns/data/tol/_ArtCollection_rubin_museum_of_himalayan_art%0A> ;
	gist:name "Mahākāla Pañjarnātha"@en ;
	.

