told:_IntellectualProperty_88
	a gist:IntellectualProperty ;
	skos:prefLabel "Taring Women"@en ;
	gist:description """<p>
	Taring Rinchen Dolma with her mother-in-law Rani Taring and her sister-in-law Kalden Wangmo. Raja Taring, Tsodrak Namgyal, of Sikkim, fled to Tibet in 1892 when the British Army entered Gangtok. He remained in Tibet, living at Taring estate near Gyantse, and later abdicating the Sikkim throne. His sons entered Tibetan government service.&nbsp;</p>
<p>
	&nbsp;</p>"""@en ;
	gist:isCategorizedBy tolx:_WorkType_photograph ;
